{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794135899,"nonce":"ur6Gjna7l7OwWWu7JG2PaBJVGds=","title":"system-ui resolves from the preloaded fonts until a system scan happens, so the Linux UI list is order-dependent","message":"Found while adding the opt-in fontconfig function (d0af0bc). FontRegistry::load_generic_with_style resolves GenericFont::System by trying the platform UI list (blinc_core::system_fonts::LINUX_SANS on Linux) against the fonts preloaded from KNOWN_FONT_PATHS only. When none match it falls to the generic sans, which also finds a preloaded face, so the lazy full system scan never runs. A family that is installed but not preloaded (Ubuntu, Cantarell, Adwaita Sans on most distros) is therefore invisible to the list until something else triggers the scan, such as a named-family miss.\n\nMeasured on the Ubuntu NUC (513 fonts, Ubuntu and Noto Sans installed): a fresh registry resolves system-ui to Noto Sans; after any scan it resolves Ubuntu, the intended face and the third entry of the list. So an app that uses plain text with no CSS family gets Noto Sans, while a cn app whose rules name a missing family first gets a scan and then Ubuntu. Scan cost on the NUC: about 15 ms with a warm file cache, about 120 ms the first time after a cold start; building the registry itself is about 0.5 ms.\n\nOptions:\n- Scan once on the first system-ui lookup. Correct for every app that uses system-ui text; costs the scan above at the first such measurement.\n- Preload more known UI-face paths. Cheap, but paths differ per distro (variable-font filenames, opentype versus truetype directories), so it stays incomplete.\n- Scan on a background thread at startup so the first lookup rarely waits. More code; moves the cost off the first frame.\n- Leave it and document that system-ui means the first listed family that is preloaded unless the app scans.\n\nThe opt-in use_fontconfig_sans already scans when its family is not preloaded, so it is not affected. Related: d0af0bc, f20f81dd.","files":null}]}